  "id": "COMPOUND:35993 - PROTEIN:6329",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Isopatriscabrol and DNA polymerase eta, mediated through the CD70 antigen. Multiple paths indicate that Isopatriscabrol targets CD70 antigen, which in turn is a target of various compounds, including Ebracteolatanolide A, 2-[(4bS,8aS,9S,10S)-1,9,10-trihydroxy-4b,8,8-trimethyl-3,4-dioxo-5,6,7,8a,9,10-hexahydrophenanthren-2-yl]propyl acetate, and 2-Isopropyl-8-methylphenanthrene-3,4-dione. These compounds all have a shared target of DNA polymerase eta, indicating a possible pathway through which Isopatriscabrol may influence DNA polymerase eta activity. The scores across all paths are consistent, suggesting a strong correlation in the evidence supporting this relationship. The mechanism appears to involve the targeting of CD70 antigen by Isopatriscabrol, which then leads to the activation or inhibition of DNA polymerase eta through the action of these compounds. The evidence is robust and consistent, but the exact nature of the interaction between Isopatriscabrol and DNA polymerase eta remains to be fully elucidated.",
